# PR #64 review round 2: fixes

Before anything: in your worktree `git merge feat/more-models` (integration branch; it now has PR #63's final state too). Tests first, gates green, commit, reply with SHA and test counts.

## Shared rules: macOS and Windows must behave identically (add tests that pin each rule)

S1 (HIGH) Gemini transcription: success only when candidates[0] exists, there's no promptFeedback.blockReason and finishReason == "STOP". Anything else (MAX_TOKENS, SAFETY, RECITATION, OTHER, missing finishReason, no candidates) is a provider failure ("Gemini didn't return a complete transcript."), whatever text came back, so the audio is kept for Retry. STOP with empty text = empty transcript.
S2 (HIGH) Transcription provider errors (ElevenLabs, Gemini, Deepgram): what reaches diagnostics/logs is only provider, model, HTTP status and a fixed reason; never response-body text. A redacted, truncated body excerpt may appear only in the user-facing error message, never in the log line. (macOS: check DictationController.describe / Diagnostics paths; Windows: dictationService + index.ts diagnostics.log.)
S3 Formatter guard parity:
  - preamble match needs a word boundary after the phrase ("i have" doesn't match "I haven't", "sure" doesn't match "Surely");
  - fillers ignored at the input start: um, umm, uh, uhh, er, erm, hmm (plus a following comma);
  - a missing stop_reason / finishReason is a failure ("truncated") on both;
  - strip "<" and ">" from dictionary words in the prompt on both.
S4 Short-dictation gate parity: unspaced scripts are Han, Hiragana, Katakana, Thai, Lao, Khmer, Myanmar (Hangul is NOT: Korean uses spaces, so words apply). For text containing them, count Unicode code points excluding whitespace, >= 6 to format. Otherwise whitespace-separated words >= 3.
S5 Formatter timeout while reading the body is logged as "timeout" (Windows gap).
S6 In-app privacy line, identical copy on both platforms, directly under the AI formatting list, shown always: "AI formatting sends each transcript to the model's provider." (No other helper text.)
S7 A stored key that can't be read (decrypt fails / Keychain locked) shows as "Add key" in its row and on models that need it, and is logged once; nothing pretends formatting is on.

